# Source, findings, commit metadata and the shifted display clock are labeled synthetic.
name: Source reassessment, causal decision order and durable Review completion
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_clock.py prepare @TMP_TARGET @ART/fixture
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/fixture/open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 DECISION SOURCE | older-source-decision
expect: 2099-01-01
expect: Reassess this verdict
expect: reassess
expect-not: NEXT open Report
ask: Does the older verdict remain readable while newer source requires Review rather than claiming Report readiness?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 DECISION SOURCE | reassessment-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 DECISION SOURCE | reassessment-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | reassessment-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | reassessment-60x20
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 ZOOM SELECTED FINDING | detail-focus
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | reassessment-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: reassessment-page-1
keys: NPage
live-snap: reassessment-page-2
keys: NPage
live-snap: reassessment-page-3
keys: NPage
live-snap: reassessment-page-4
keys: NPage
live-snap: reassessment-page-5
ask: Can the operator read the older verdict and source warning at 40x12 while the journey remains in Review?
resize: 120x36
keys: PPage
require-live-snap: 20 recorded: confirmed | older-clock-verdict
submit: decision deferred Synthetic source B deliberately deferred
require-live-snap: 30 No later observation | newer-causal-decision
expect: recorded: deferred
expect: Synthetic source B deliberately deferred
expect: fixture-b
expect: NEXT open Report
ask: Does the explicit new decision govern source B despite the old future display date, with the earlier decision retained and no fix claim?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/fixture/open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Synthetic source B deliberately deferred | source-restarted
expect: fixture-b
expect: No later observation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/review_clock.py verify @TMP_TARGET @ART/fixture
ask: Does no-color restart agree with export about the new source-qualified decision while preserving all earlier provenance and source bytes?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
